1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,050
Welcome to Green Vale Agricultural Park.

2
00:00:03,050 --> 00:00:08,220
As you know, we have only been open a week so you are amongst our first visitors.

3
00:00:08,220 --> 00:00:11,060
We have lots of fascinating indoor

4
00:00:11,060 --> 00:00:15,060
and outdoor exhibits on our huge complex, spreading hundreds of hectares.

5
00:00:15,060 --> 00:00:20,200
Our remit is to give educational opportunities to the wider public

6
00:00:20,520 --> 00:00:26,780
as well as to offer research sites for a wide variety of agriculturists and other scientists.

7
00:00:26,780 --> 00:00:30,190
Let's start by seeing what there is to do.

8
00:00:30,190 --> 00:00:34,860
As you can see here on our giant wall plan

9
00:00:35,160 --> 00:00:38,260
we are now situated in the Reception block O... here.

10
00:00:38,260 --> 00:00:43,860
As you walk out of the main door into the park there is a path you can follow.

11
00:00:43,860 --> 00:00:48,255
If you follow this route you will immediately come into the Rare Breeds section,

12
00:00:48,255 --> 00:00:51,560
where we keep a wide variety of animals

13
00:00:51,600 --> 00:00:54,220
which I shall be telling you a little more about later.

14
00:00:54,220 --> 00:01:01,000
Next to this, moving east, is the large grazing area for the rare breeds.

15
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:06,630
Then further east, in the largest section of our Park is the Forest Area.

16
00:01:06,630 --> 00:01:08,920
South of the grazing area

17
00:01:08,980 --> 00:01:12,780
and in fact just next to the Reception block is our Experimental Crop Area.

18
00:01:12,780 --> 00:01:15,540
In the middle of the Park

19
00:01:15,740 --> 00:01:21,516
this circular area is our lake These two small rectangular shapes here,

20
00:01:21,516 --> 00:01:26,370
are the Fish Farms where we rear fish for sale.

21
00:01:26,370 --> 00:01:32,820
To the east of those is the marsh area which attracts a great many migrant birds.

22
00:01:32,820 --> 00:01:36,720
In the south-eastern corner, beyond the marsh

23
00:01:36,880 --> 00:01:40,910
is our Market Garden area, growing vegetables and flowers.

24
00:01:40,910 --> 00:01:47,375
All these areas can be visited by the general public for almost all the year, although...

25
00:01:47,375 --> 00:01:53,436
please take note of the large signs at the entrance to each area which tell,

26
00:01:53,436 --> 00:01:58,689
which tell you when certain areas are being used for particular controlled experiments

27
00:01:58,689 --> 00:02:02,730
and are therefore temporarily out of bounds to the public.

28
00:02:02,730 --> 00:02:07,630
You can see for yourself what a huge area the park covers

29
00:02:08,353 --> 00:02:12,370
and a key question is always, how can we move around

30
00:02:12,370 --> 00:02:14,880
Well you have a choice of means

31
00:02:15,160 --> 00:02:19,330
all environmentally friendly, cars are banned in the park.

32
00:02:19,330 --> 00:02:23,867
We have bicycles which you can hire behind the Reception block, here,

33
00:02:23,867 --> 00:02:26,380
the healthy ones of you can go on foot

34
00:02:26,820 --> 00:02:31,050
and finally there's our electric tram, powered from solar cells.

35
00:02:31,050 --> 00:02:33,940
You find more information about this at the front entrance.

36
00:02:33,940 --> 00:02:38,880
A good place to start on your tour is the Rare Breeds section.

37
00:02:38,880 --> 00:02:43,060
We keep goats, sheep and hens and other kinds of poultry.

38
00:02:43,060 --> 00:02:47,387
We are also thinking of bringing in cows and horses but we do not,

39
00:02:47,387 --> 00:02:49,860
as yet, have facilities for these bigger animals.

40
00:02:49,860 --> 00:02:53,383
The animals are fed in public twice a day

41
00:02:53,383 --> 00:02:58,080
and a short lecture given on their feeding habits and nutritional needs.

42
00:02:58,080 --> 00:03:00,560
These are very popular with the public

43
00:03:00,560 --> 00:03:05,875
but of course we mustn't lose sight of the main purpose of having this section,

44
00:03:05,875 --> 00:03:08,355
not as such to preserve rare animals

45
00:03:08,355 --> 00:03:10,120
but to maintain the diversity of breeds

46
00:03:10,520 --> 00:03:13,670
to broaden the gene pool for agricultural development.

47
00:03:13,670 --> 00:03:17,020
Green Vale changes with the seasons

48
00:03:17,200 --> 00:03:19,770
with different events happening at different times of the year.

49
00:03:19,770 --> 00:03:25,629
May will be perhaps our most spectacular month with the arrival of the Canada geese

50
00:03:25,629 --> 00:03:28,520
and when our fruit trees will be in full blossom

51
00:03:28,520 --> 00:03:33,051
but there are interesting events on all year round,

52
00:03:33,051 --> 00:03:36,620
for example John Havers, our expert fly fisherman

53
00:03:36,880 --> 00:03:38,910
is currently giving displays on the lake.

54
00:03:38,910 --> 00:03:46,340
Each of the sections has its own seasonal calendar, please consult the summary board at the main entrance.

55
00:03:46,340 --> 00:03:51,330
And the final section, as we return to the Reception blocks, is the orchard.

56
00:03:51,330 --> 00:03:57,125
Do take time to browse round our shop, there is a wide selection of books on wildlife,

57
00:03:57,125 --> 00:04:01,216
some of them written by local authors, and the history of farming,

58
00:04:01,216 --> 00:04:06,330
including organic farming, something which the park will be diversifying into in the coming months.
